    "result_text": "The build is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of a future `registrationDate` on `POST /api/owners`, following the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions in this repo (not Spring MVC controllers).\n\n**New files:**\n- `ValidateOwnerRegistrationDate.java` \u2014 a validation step reading the already-published `@Val OwnerFieldsDto`. If `registrationDate` is supplied and `isAfter(LocalDate.now())`, it throws `FutureRegistrationDateException`. The field is optional, so `null` passes through (it defaults to the server date at build time).\n- `FutureRegistrationDateException.java` \u2014 a checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause for escalation matching.\n- `FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds **400** with a JSON `errors` body, mirroring the existing `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler`.\n- `officefloor/escalation/...FutureRegistrationDateException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to the handler.\n\n**Wiring:** inserted a `validateRegistrationDate` step into `owners.POST.yml` right after `validatePostcode` \u2014 early, before any persistence work, consistent with the other pre-flight 400 validations.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsFutureDate` (posting `registrationDate: \"2999-01-01\"` and expecting 400) passes, and the full test suite is green.",
